From: RLtools <rl-tools@localhost>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] [libc++abi] Provide __cxa_thread_atexit on WASI

thread_local objects with destructors register them through
__cxa_thread_atexit, which libc++abi defined only for Linux and Fuchsia.
The fallback implementation needs nothing more than the pthread key
functions and __cxa_atexit, both of which wasi-libc provides (its keys
are plain globals in a single-threaded build), so WASI joins the list.
Without it a link that keeps such an object, for example lld's ELF port
under ThinLTO, fails with an undefined symbol.
---
 libcxxabi/src/cxa_thread_atexit.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libcxxabi/src/cxa_thread_atexit.cpp b/libcxxabi/src/cxa_thread_atexit.cpp
index 402a52c74..ea89488d1 100644
--- a/libcxxabi/src/cxa_thread_atexit.cpp
+++ b/libcxxabi/src/cxa_thread_atexit.cpp
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ namespace {
 
 #endif // HAVE___CXA_THREAD_ATEXIT_IMPL
 
-#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__Fuchsia__)
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__Fuchsia__) || defined(__wasi__)
 extern "C" {
 
   _LIBCXXABI_FUNC_VIS int __cxa_thread_atexit(Dtor dtor, void* obj, void* dso_symbol) throw() {
@@ -142,5 +142,5 @@ extern "C" {
 #endif // HAVE___CXA_THREAD_ATEXIT_IMPL
   }
 } // extern "C"
-#endif // defined(__linux__) || defined(__Fuchsia__)
+#endif // defined(__linux__) || defined(__Fuchsia__) || defined(__wasi__)
 } // namespace __cxxabiv1
